SUMMARY:Introduction to bikepacking 101 (37 R)
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Bicycle Club (LBC) Meetup\nRide Leader: Bruce Black\
 n\nAn introduction to bikepacking. This is a 37-mile route with an overnig
 ht camping experience at Starlight campground in Clay\, PA. We will start 
 in Lititz with a gear check and loading onto bicycles. From Lititz\, we wi
 ll make our way to Foxmill Creamery (about 10 miles into the ride) in Clay
  for an afternoon snack. From there\, we will head into the gamelands for 
 some gravel riding as we make our way to the campsite at roughly the 20-mi
 le mark. **YOU WILL WANT TO RIDE A BIKE THAT IS CAPABLE OF RIDING ON GRAVE
 L.** After a restful night of sleeping under the stars\, we will pack up a
 nd head back to Lititz\, stopping at a coffee shop along the way. Plan on 
 cooking a meal for dinner and for breakfast. This will test out your camps
 ite cooking setup and food choices. Please check out the [Bikepacking 101 
 gear list](https://bikepacking.com/bikepacking-101/pack-list/) for some id
 eas on what to bring and how to set up your bike. Another good reference i
 s the following YouTube video: [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zH4NOPWZxG
 U](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zH4NOPWZxGU)\n\n**ALL RIDERS ARE RESPON
 SIBLE FOR THEIR OWN GEAR AND FOOD. YOU ARE GOING TO WANT A GRAVEL BIKE FOR
  THIS RIDE.**\n\nThe idea of this trip is to test out the gear setup on th
 e bike and camping in preparation for riding the Great Allegheny Passage a
 nd C&O Canal paths from Pittsburgh to Washington\, DC.\n\nIf you have any 
 questions please message me.\n\nThis ride is a social ride\, but cyclists 
 are not expected to stay in one group. Cyclists may pedal at their own com
 fortable paces. Please be supportive of the other cyclists to avoid anyone
  biking alone or being dropped off the back of the last group.\n\nCue and 
 Ride with GPS links:\n[https://ridewithgps.com/routes/53501875](https://ri
 dewithgps.com/routes/53501875)\n\nHelmets are mandatory\; please also plan
  to bring 1-2 water bottles\, and a basic repair kit (spare tube\, tire le
 vers\, pump/CO2 inflator).\nBeing a Meetup Member does not mean you are a 
 club member. Use this link to join the club.\n[https://www.lancasterbikecl
 ub.net/content.aspx?page_id=60&club_id=257148](https://www.lancasterbikecl
 ub.net/content.aspx?page_id=60&club_id=257148)\nYour RSVP is your agreemen
 t to abide by the club's Code of Conduct [https://lancbikeclub.clubexpress
 .com/content.aspx?page_id=22&club_id=257148&module_id=323984](https://lanc
 bikeclub.clubexpress.com/content.aspx?page_id=22&club_id=257148&module_id=
 323984)\nand Rules of the Road\n[https://lancbikeclub.clubexpress.com/cont
 ent.aspx?](https://lancbikeclub.clubexpress.com/content.aspx?page_id=22&cl
 ub_id=257148&module_id=325159)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/lancaster-bicycle-club/events/3131925
 06/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260203T192729Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260203T192729Z
